IMPORT prelude
IMPORT fip

-- Cases for fip.l4. Every expected value was worked out by hand from the deposited text of Human Services ss 5-308,
-- 5-312, 5-313 and 5-315, not copied from the encoding's output. Grant amounts are invented (the real ones are set in
-- COMAR, not deposited).
--
-- Argument order of `Can my family get temporary cash assistance`: minor child, pregnant, live in Maryland, child support
-- cooperation, child support good cause, doing work activity, care for baby, severely disabled, months exempt for
-- disability, SSI application, no assistance for 6 months, other requirements met, assign support, minor parent, minor
-- parent arrangement, months of TCA, hardship exemption, immigrant after 1996, eligible for federal cash assistance.

§ `Cases`

§§ `Eligibility (ss 5-308, 5-312(b), 5-313)`

-- A single mother with a 3-year-old, living in Maryland, cooperating with child support, in job search, assigning support,
-- 10 months of TCA so far: entitled.
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: my family meets the conditions of ss 5-308(a) and 5-312(b), so it is entitled to temporary cash assistance (s 5-312(c)), at the amount the regulations set`
-- A pregnant woman with no children, otherwise the same: s 5-308(a)(2)(ii), entitled.
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: my family meets the conditions of ss 5-308(a) and 5-312(b), so it is entitled to temporary cash assistance (s 5-312(c)), at the amount the regulations set`
-- An adult with no child and no pregnancy: not a family under s 5-308(a)(2).
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the family must include a minor child living with a custodial parent or adult caretaker relative, or a pregnant individual (s 5-308(a)(2))`
-- Moved out of Maryland before applying: s 5-308(a)(3)(i).
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I must reside in Maryland when I apply (s 5-308(a)(3)(i))`
-- Not cooperating with child support, but fear of violence from the other parent (good cause, s 5-308(d)(3)(i)): entitled.
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: my family meets the conditions of ss 5-308(a) and 5-312(b), so it is entitled to temporary cash assistance (s 5-312(c)), at the amount the regulations set`
-- Not cooperating and no good cause: refused under (a)(3)(ii).
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I must apply for child support services and comply with the child support office, unless I have good cause or an adequate reason (s 5-308(a)(3)(ii), (d), (e))`
-- No work activity, but caring for a baby under 1 in the case: exempt, entitled.
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: my family meets the conditions of ss 5-308(a) and 5-312(b), so it is entitled to temporary cash assistance (s 5-312(c)), at the amount the regulations set`
-- No work activity, severely disabled and exempt for 12 months already, no SSI application: no longer exempt; refused.
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 12 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I must take part in work activity, unless I am exempt (s 5-308(a)(3)(iii), (b))`
-- Fails the regulatory requirements (for example the income test in COMAR): s 5-308(a)(3)(iv).
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I must meet the other FIP requirements set by regulation (s 5-308(a)(3)(iv))`
-- Not assigning support: s 5-312(b)(2).
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I must assign my rights to child support to the State while we receive TCA (s 5-312(b)(2))`
-- A 16-year-old mother living alone with no social worker confirmation: s 5-312(b)(3).
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: as a minor parent I must live with an adult relative payee, in an adult-supervised group home, or independently where a social worker confirms it is needed (s 5-312(b)(3))`
-- 61 months of TCA, no hardship exemption: s 5-313(a)(1). With a hardship exemption: entitled.
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 61 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an adult in my family has received more than 60 months of federally funded TCA and the family has no hardship exemption (s 5-313(a)(1))`
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 61 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: my family meets the conditions of ss 5-308(a) and 5-312(b), so it is entitled to temporary cash assistance (s 5-312(c)), at the amount the regulations set`
-- 30 months, exempt (caring for a baby) and so not in work activity: s 5-313(a)(2) still bars payment (NOTES.md finding 1).
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an adult in my family has received more than 24 months of federally funded TCA and is not participating in a work activity (s 5-313(a)(2))`
-- A legal immigrant who arrived in 2001 and is eligible for federally funded cash assistance: not entitled under s 5-308(h).
#ASSERT `Can my family get temporary cash assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: a legal immigrant who arrived on or after 22 August 1996 and is eligible for federally funded cash assistance is not entitled under s 5-308(h)`

§§ `Exemptions (s 5-308(b))`

-- Argument order: care for baby, severely disabled, months exempt for disability, SSI application, no assistance for 6 months.
#ASSERT `Am I exempt from work activity` TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I exempt from work activity` FALSE TRUE 11 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Am I exempt from work activity` FALSE TRUE 12 FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `Am I exempt from work activity` FALSE TRUE 18 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I exempt from work activity` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Am I exempt from work activity` FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE))

§§ `Hours (s 5-308(a)(4), (6))`

#ASSERT `How many hours of work activity may be required of me` "single parent with a child under 6" FALSE EQUALS `hours` 20
#ASSERT `How many hours of work activity may be required of me` "parent with a child at least 6" FALSE EQUALS `hours` 30
#ASSERT `How many hours of work activity may be required of me` "two parents without child care" FALSE EQUALS `hours` 35
#ASSERT `How many hours of work activity may be required of me` "two parents with child care" FALSE EQUALS `hours` 55
#ASSERT `How many hours of work activity may be required of me` "two parents with child care" TRUE EQUALS `not stated, because an adult in the family has a disability or cares for a child with a disability, so (iv) does not apply (s 5-308(a)(6)(iv))`
#ASSERT `Does my education count as work activity` 20 0 FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Does my education count as work activity` 19 0 FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Does my education count as work activity` 25 24 FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Does my education count as work activity` 25 3 TRUE))

§§ `Sanctions (s 5-312(e))`

-- Grant $700, adults' portion $250. Work noncompliance: 30% x 250 = 75, so 625. Child support noncompliance: 25% x 700 =
-- 175, so 525. Both: 700 - 75 - 175 = 450. Complied since: 700.
#ASSERT `How much TCA will I get after a sanction` 700 250 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 625
#ASSERT `How much TCA will I get after a sanction` 700 250 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 525
#ASSERT `How much TCA will I get after a sanction` 700 250 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 450
#ASSERT `How much TCA will I get after a sanction` 700 250 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `How long before my TCA can be cut` EQUALS 30

-- The Department makes no cut until day 31: the s 5-312(e)(4) bar is respected.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 5-312(e)(4) -- no reduction or termination until 30 days after the first written notice` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Department` `reduce or terminate the family's temporary cash assistance` 31)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH by the Department -- the grant is cut on day 12, within the 30 days.
#TRACE `s 5-312(e)(4) -- no reduction or termination until 30 days after the first written notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Department` DOES `reduce or terminate the family's temporary cash assistance` AT 12
-- The recipient complies on day 20 of the conciliation period: fulfilled, no reduction.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 5-312(e)(3) -- I may comply within the 30-day conciliation period, failing which my assistance may be reduced` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the recipient` `comply with the FIP requirement` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- The recipient does not comply; on day 40 the Department reduces the grant, as it then may: fulfilled, not a breach.
-- (The event on day 35 only moves the clock past day 30; it is not matched against the rule that follows.)
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 5-312(e)(3) -- I may comply within the 30-day conciliation period, failing which my assistance may be reduced` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Department` `reduce or terminate the family's temporary cash assistance` 35), (EVENT `the Department` `reduce or terminate the family's temporary cash assistance` 40)) EQUALS FULFILLED

§§ `Transitional assistance and SSI`

#ASSERT `How many months of transitional assistance` TRUE EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `How many months of transitional assistance` FALSE EQUALS 0
-- $1,200 of family income including $900 of a child's SSI: $300 counts.
#ASSERT `How much income counts for FIP eligibility` 1200 900 EQUALS 300
